    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 honda civic makes this loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be the serpentine belt or something? can u explain what that belt actually does and why it would make a screeching sound like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A serpentine belt, or drive belt, is a crucial part of your engine's operation, as it transfers power from the engine's crankshaft to various accessories. These accessories include the alternator (which charges the battery), the power steering pump, and the water pump. If the belt is worn, loose, or if one of the pulleys it drives is failing, it can certainly produce a loud squealing noise when you apply throttle. It's a common issue, and it's a good idea to have a mechanic take a look at it soon before it causes a bigger problem.",
