    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds scary. i dont want to be stranded on the highway. is there any way to tell if it's just the belt or if something else is wrong before it actually breaks? like are there any specific signs i should look for besides the noise?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can look for several telltale signs that suggest a problem beyond just a simple squeak. Besides the noise, watch for any visible fraying, cracking, or glazing on the belt itself, which indicates wear. If the belt seems unusually loose or if you notice excessive vibration in the engine bay, that's another red flag. Also, if your battery light starts flashing or your car begins to overheat, those are clear signs that the belt's function is compromised. It's best to inspect it when the engine is cool, if possible.",
      "source": "target",
